                        "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                        "entry_id": "9c377bf0-737d-3549-a137-29b807f1662f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of forked."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db9e6fc2-29da-45f1-ba86-591fde3adf8d",
                                "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                                "text": "[…] for hungry birds have devoured ſeeds, and having moiſtened and warmed them in their bellies, a little after have dunged in the forky twiſtes of Trees, and together with their dung excluded the ſeed whole which erſt they had ſwallowed: and ſometimes it brings forth there where they dung it, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ea00ff3-d815-4e0c-857d-63ff6c467dcb",
                                "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                                "text": "The Leaves are compoſed each of ſeven parts; the Flowers grow by two's on forky Footſtalks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b074caa1-0b78-47be-9403-46a0e49ddbd2",
                                "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                                "text": "The forky lightning flashed, and the deep toned thunder reverberated peal on peal, while the shrieking winds rocked the tree tops, and poured their wild melody upon the ear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e29cf3f6-d70c-4647-a07b-bd7f4cdf22f2",
                                "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                                "text": "The column of fire now ascended above the main-top—licking with its forky tongue the top-mast rigging—and embracing the mainmast in its folds: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71e32010-6741-45c8-982b-e2966d599a27",
                                "sense_id": "ca55cdba-bd15-3cfb-bd3a-ce2e6d9b9fce",
                                "text": "At the sight of the young man it lashed its tail so violently that the earth trembled as if with an earthquake, while its forky tongue darted in and out with a deafening hissing noise."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
